insert into marketing_needs (id, property_id, title, description, category, urgency, budget_band, status, dataset) values
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001','Social media & digital agency partner for Sapphire House Antwerp (OHG tender)','Odyssey Hotel Group is appointing a social media and digital agency to act as an extension of the internal marketing team for Sapphire House Antwerp and selected properties. Scope: Meta posting, content direction and community management; LinkedIn organic; paid media on Meta, LinkedIn and Google Ads (budgets set per hotel); Google Business Profile optimisation; performance monitoring and monthly reporting (reach, engagement, CTR, CPC, conversions, budget usage); influencer identification and coordination; content updates on vanity websites; quarterly photoshoots for the hotel and restaurant with creative direction and production coordination. Language requirements may differ between English, Dutch, Spanish and German. Required: a dedicated account manager, named social resources, a paid media specialist, a Google Ads specialist, holiday cover and escalation contacts, and full transfer of IP on payment (non-negotiable). Proposal deadline 9 September 2026.','social','high','15k+','open','real'),
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001','Monthly photo and video content production for Sapphire House and Sapphire Patio','Alongside the social media partnership the hotel wants a structural monthly supply of on-brand photo and video: one shoot day per month delivering around 100 photos with RAW selection and retouching, 2 cinematic reels and 3 iPhone reels, filmed with cinema camera, gimbal and drone in rotation, creative direction on site, a quarterly highlight reel, delivery within 5 working days via a dedicated drive. Formats considered: Essential (1,550 EUR/month), Editorial (2,200 EUR/month) or quarterly (2,750 EUR/quarter).','content','normal','1-5k','open','real'),
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005','Annual Report 2026 photography across the five Brussels Pandox properties','Pandox Belgium needs an editorial photo stock for its 2026 Annual Report, shot in one intensive day across Holiday Inn Brussels Airport, Hotel Indigo, DoubleTree by Hilton (construction site), Hilton Brussels Grand Place and The Hotel Brussels. Six themes: hotel life, work and operations, DEI woven through all scenes, sustainability, construction, spa. Style must match the AR 2025 language: warm 4200-4800K golden tones, subtle sepia, filmic grain, people in action never posed. Deliverables: 25-35 images shot, about 30 final edits, TIFF 300 dpi and web JPG, model releases for all staff, full IP transfer, delivery within 7 working days of selection. / Pandox Belgique a besoin d''un fonds photographique editorial pour le Rapport Annuel 2026, tourne en une journee dans les cinq proprietes bruxelloises. Six themes, tons dores chauds, personnes en action jamais posees, cession totale des droits.','photography','high',null,'open','real'),
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006','Code of Conduct training video (3-4 min) for the Pandox Compliance Platform','A 3-4 minute branded video for Pandox''s internal Code of Conduct training module: new footage filmed at The Hotel or Hilton Grand Place, integrated seamlessly into an existing video whose Aldert Schaaphok segment is retained as-is. Speakers: a senior leadership message (about 1 min), one speaker to confirm, and authentic on-the-ground testimonials from Brussels hotel employees. Sony A7V, 2.4K to match existing footage, colour grade precisely matched, lower thirds from Pandox brand assets, sound design and music, 2 revision rounds included. / Video de marque de 3-4 minutes pour le module de formation interne Code de Conduite: nouveau footage integre a une video existante, etalonnage correspondant, coaching des intervenants sur place.','content','normal','1-5k','open','real'),
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000007','RAIBU Gent launch: main reel plus vertical snippets','One main reel for the new RAIBU location in Ghent, carrying a single arc from the chaos of the city outside (traffic lights, sirens, rush) to the calm inside once the door opens, plus a series of vertical snippets cut from the same scenes and captured live on the shoot day, for social, advertising and OTA. The guest journey (pin-code check-in, hallway with suitcase, room without model, tea, shower, covers) is shot as larger scenes and split in the edit. Look: VHS texture meeting clean digital, nostalgic but legible, cinematic never stock. One production day in Ghent; styling and set dressing by STAY-C; consistent RAIBU branding, grade and sound design.','content','normal',null,'open','real'),
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000008','STAY-C corporate film and reusable content library','A company film about STAY-C as a hospitality operator, balancing three strands without letting one dominate: management (who STAY-C is, expertise, approach), properties (the six brands and buildings as proof, RAIBU as one example), organisation (people, service, operations). For sales, investors, partners, recruitment and web. One production day, ample b-roll across both STAY-C shoots to build a reusable library of video and bulk photography. Tone reference: STAY-C reel DVIkBEQgGd8.','content','normal',null,'open','real'),
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000007','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009','Refresh van de visuele identiteit: hero film, vier UGC-capsules en fotopakket (Elk zijn tempo)','Cocoon Hotel La Rive wil in een draaidag zes deliverables realiseren: een hero film ''Elk zijn tempo'' (60-75 s, 16:9 en 9:16) die het hotel op twee ritmes toont (rust van de trouwe oudere gasten, energie van jonge koppels: fiets, tuin, Sure, lange tafel bij gouden uur), vier UGC-capsules (20-30 s, 9:16) met de manager, de chef, wellness (sauna, hammam) en de behandelcabines, en een fotopakket van 15-20 geretoucheerde beelden voor website, OTA-profielen, Google Business en brochure. Geen modellen: echte medewerkers en gasten, gasten enkel niet-identificeerbaar tenzij toestemming. Taal: UGC in het Frans gesproken met Engelse ondertitels; als Frans niet lukt, Engels met Franse ondertitels. Commercieel doel: de perceptiekloof sluiten (stille bestemming voor senioren versus oase van natuur, wellness en gastronomie), jongere koppels winnen zonder de trouwe basis te verliezen, en directe boekingen stimuleren. Team: fotograaf, videograaf, dronepiloot. Volledige gebruiksrechten, levering binnen 5 werkdagen.','content','high',null,'open','real'),
  ('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000008','e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004','Brand film ''Where Time Waits'' (1''30) and 30-second meetings & events capsule','Le Palace / DoubleTree by Hilton Brussels City wants a 1''30 cinematic presentation film and one 30-second capsule covering four locations (restaurant and bar, meeting rooms, guest rooms and suites, fitness and sauna) for website, YouTube, LinkedIn and corporate screens. Business objective: reposition the hotel as a living heritage conference destination and visually communicate its transformation to event planners and corporate clients; many markets still hold older perceptions. Creative constraints: 100% cinematic, architecture as central character, real DoubleTree employees in light non-speaking roles, no explanatory voice-over, avoid the commercial register and generic hotel cliches. Production budget 2,000 EUR incl. VAT firm for one shoot day (crew, lead actor, styling, drone shot of the facade matching a 1910 photograph), post-production separate. / Un film de presentation cinematographique de 1''30 et une capsule de 30 secondes sur quatre espaces; objectif: repositionner l''hotel centenaire comme destination de conferences vivante; budget de production 2 000 EUR TTC ferme, tournage en une journee, drone sur la facade.','content','high','1-5k','open','real')
insert into documents (org_id, property_id, kind, title, body, source) values
  ('e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',null,'brief','OHG tender: social media & digital agency services (28 Aug 2026)','Odyssey Hotel Group operates a diverse portfolio of hotels and hospitality brands across Europe, HQ Utrecht (NL). The agency will support multiple brands and properties, each with different brand guidelines, target audiences, commercial needs and content requirements. Objective: ongoing social execution on Meta and LinkedIn; paid social; Google Ads and Google Business optimisation; performance tracking and monthly reporting; content planning, community management, audience growth; influencer relationships; vanity website updates (premium brands only); quarterly photoshoots for selected properties incl. Sapphire House Antwerp; act as a proactive digital partner and understand the region. Account structure: dedicated account manager, named digital and social resources, paid media specialist, Google Ads specialist, community management, influencer contact, website/digital contact, photoshoot/production coordination contact, senior strategic oversight, holiday cover, escalation contacts. Service requirements: multi-brand experience, cases in hospitality, multi-property groups, lifestyle/premium brands, paid social, Google Ads, LinkedIn, influencer, website support, reporting; indicative turnaround times per work type; review and approval workflow incl. multi-hotel stakeholder approvals. Reporting: monthly report with organic, paid, Google Ads, Google Business, LinkedIn, website and influencer performance, budget usage, learnings and next steps. IP: all creative work becomes exclusive property of OHG on payment, editable source files delivered, no ongoing licensing; agencies not accepting this are not considered. Proposal must include company profile, proposed account team and retainer hours, monthly deliverables, approach per channel, reporting approach and example report, cases and three client references, pricing, additional charges, contract and cancellation terms. Submission deadline 9 September 2026.','drive/Sapphire House Antwerp/OHG Social Media Agency Tender Document_Sapphire House Antwep (1).pdf'),
  (null,'e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001','proposal','Hautel content production proposal for Sapphire House Antwerp (Jun 2026)','Hautel is a hospitality marketing agency bringing together content, strategy and AI automation for hotels, working as an extension of the hotel team with a dedicated personal drive. Behind every production stands a full creative team: videographers, photographers, creative directors, drone pilots, designers and specialists in fashion and influencer content. Offer alongside the ongoing social media partnership: a flexible content package. Per shoot day: 100 composed photos, full RAW delivery for selection, professional colour grading and retouching, 2 cinematic reels, 3 iPhone reels, trend research and creative proposals, on-brand visual language. Formats: Essential 1 day/month 1,550 EUR; Editorial 1 day/month 2,200 EUR (100+ photos, 4 cinematic reels, cinema/gimbal/drone, stronger art direction); Quarterly 2,750 EUR/quarter; On Demand for employer branding, campaigns, modelling, events or UGC. Included: brand and content analysis, creative direction on site, usage rights for the hotel''s own channels, delivery within 5 working days. Add-ons: AI dubbing, editing of existing imagery, travel outside Antwerp, external locations, props, styling, music licences, subtitles, translations. Onboarding via shared Google Drive and role-based access to LinkedIn, Canva, Meta Business and Google, no password sharing; supplementary terms cover GDPR and privacy.','drive/Sapphire House Antwerp/Hautel_Content_Offer_Sapphire_House_EN.pdf'),
  ('e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002',null,'positioning','About the client: Pandox Belgium (project briefing 2025/2026)','Pandox AB is a leading hotel property company listed on Nasdaq Stockholm, founded 1995, owning and leasing over 150 hotel properties in Europe and North America with operators including Hilton, Marriott, IHG and Hyatt. Belgium properties: Holiday Inn Brussels Airport, Hotel Indigo, DoubleTree by Hilton (under construction), Hilton Brussels Grand Place, The Hotel Brussels. Business model: hotel property ownership plus long-term revenue-based leases with guaranteed minimum. Core values: collaboration, curiosity, courage, competence, clarity. Focus areas: property management, property development, portfolio optimisation, sustainability. ESG: 86% of own-operation hotels have locally adapted targets for socially marginalised groups; science-based sustainability targets active. Brand palette from the Annual Report 2025: charcoal, gold, deep teal, burgundy, warm gold, sand, cream, warm grey. Photo style requirements: colour temperature 4200-4800K, warm golden undertones never cold digital blue; editorial framing with room to breathe; people in action, never posed, human but discreet; available light preferred; avoid cold tones, heavy saturation, direct flash, stock-photo poses. Working languages of the briefing: English and French.','drive/PANDOX - Project 2026/pandox_project_briefing.pdf'),
  ('e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002',null,'brief','Pandox Belgium Annual Report 2026: creative masterfile and shotlists (May 2026)','The visual atmosphere must read as a premium editorial documentary, never commercial advertising; human authenticity and operational truth. Capture: warm golden tones, ambient natural light, subtle sepia editorial treatment, cinematic framing, quiet luxury, real people and real operations. Avoid: corporate posing, fluorescent light, heavy saturation, staged environments, heavy retouching. Target grade: warm highlights, rich dark-brown shadows, saturation reduced 10-15%, medium-high contrast, candlelight colour cast. Hotel Indigo Brussels (human rights, DEI, well-being): housekeeping in action, trolley in corridor, sustainable cleaning products, team diversity, employee well-being, Vajra breakfast refill, Shower Challenge QR, Varga circularity, BIGH sprouts and fish filleting. DoubleTree by Hilton Brussels (energy efficiency, renovation, smart tools, sustainable F&B): new facade at golden hour, construction site with PPE, maintenance with iPad, HVAC/CHP plant room, electric kitchen with Winnow, brasserie, submetering tablet, HotelGPT by Juyo Analytics, heat pump, first aid kit, supplier collaboration, MSC/ASC and fair-trade sourcing. Hilton Brussels Grand Place (guest experience, inclusive culture, smart operations): lobby, front office welcome, meeting room domotics, bar and restaurant, Clean the World, Too Good To Go, Hope & Glory teas, solar panels, BMS/Sensorea, Climato, Enozo, bike in the office. The Hotel Brussels (well-being, sustainable hospitality, quiet luxury): spa pool, wellness details, Brussels panorama at dusk, architectural frames, AI tools in-room, BIGH sprouts. Across hotels: thermostat and CO2 detector, waste sorting, Fresk training, Sensorea t-shirts, housekeeping portraits, Run To Kick, Joie de Vivre interns, BREEAM signage, coaching moments. Technical: RAW mandatory, 24 MP minimum for double-page spreads, TIFF plus web JPEG, model releases for all identifiable individuals, selects in 5 working days, finals 15 working days after approval. Shoot schedule: two days, 23-24 September 2026 preferred (alt 28-29), Indigo and DoubleTree on day 1, Hilton Grand Place and The Hotel on day 2.','drive/PANDOX - Project 2026/Annual Report: Photography/Pandox_Creative_Masterfile_2026_EN.pdf; Pandox_2Day_Shoot_Schedule (2).docx'),
  ('e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003',null,'brief','Hautel x STAY-C project briefing v3.0 (2026)','STAY-C is a fast-growing hospitality operator: six brands (A-STAY urban city hotel, RAIBU apart-hotels, ROMY short-term rentals, PATTY hospitality concept, JACKEY student housing, XEPA hospitality concept), 1000+ units across Belgium, 300+ more in the pipeline. Founded 2020 by Eduard Van Nevel and Anthony Vancauwenberghe; 2024 acquisition of A-STAY Hotel Antwerp; 2025 launch of RAIBU in Ghent and Antwerp; 2026 launch of JACKEY. Operator, not a landlord: develops concepts, manages operations, builds brands. Digital-first ecosystem: keyless check-in, AI guest comms, dynamic pricing, owner portal. Design-led and consistent: distinct brand identities, one operational standard. Two video projects with one quality standard and two visual worlds, never confused in edit. Project 1 RAIBU Gent (brown world): main reel from city chaos to calm inside plus snippets; guest journey arrival (pin-code check-in, entering, elevator, hallway with suitcase, jacket set down, room without model) and settling in (washing hands, tea or coffee, chair out, plates into dishwasher, shower, curtains, covers); look mixes VHS texture and clean digital; references ALOHAS, The Standard Brussels, Sonder, RAIBU LHS mood deck. Project 2 STAY-C corporate film: management, properties, organisation in balance; possible flow intro (hospitality is changing), who, the brands, approach, close (not managing buildings but creating hospitality experiences). Deliverables: one production day each, main reel plus vertical snippets and ample b-roll; one film plus reusable library of video and bulk photo. Process: alignment, pre-production, production (2 days), post (edit, grade, sound), delivery plus library. Pricing, deliverable counts and usage rights in a separate quotation. STAY-C HQ Soenenspark 1, 9051 Gent; Antwerp Italielei 183.','drive/Stay C x RAIBU Shoot/HAUTEL_x_STAYC_Briefing.pdf'),
  (null,'e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009','brief','Cocoon Hotels: To Each Their Tempo, creative proposal (2026, EN)','Cocoon Hotel La Rive is a recently renovated four-star property on the banks of the Sure at Bourscheid-Plage, Luxembourg: 19 rooms, 12 cottage suites and one villa, a health centre with sauna and hammam, a riverside restaurant. Today seen as a peaceful destination for an older clientele; that image rests on loyal returning guests but hides that the same setting suits an active getaway: cycling, walks along the Sure, wellness, long shared tables, an audience of younger couples Cocoon struggles to win. Perception gap: quiet destination for seniors vs oasis of nature, wellness and fine dining; a mere stopover vs a whole weekend; nothing to do but rest vs cycling, walks, sauna, hammam, river; voucher-driven clientele vs a direct audience of active couples. Mission: close the gap without saying it, win younger couples without alienating the loyal base, drive direct bookings. Package, one shooting day: hero film ''To Each Their Tempo'' 60-75 s 16:9 and 9:16; four UGC capsules 20-30 s 9:16 (the manager ''everything in its place'', the head chef ''the chef who tastes everything'', wellness ''how NOT to relax'', the treatment cabins ''the ranking''); website photo pack 15-20 retouched photos. Concept: the relay of gesture, a calm gesture by an older guest completed more intensely by a young couple. Six movements: the valley awakens, the slow world, the first relay, the active world, the tempos meet at the long dinner table at golden hour, the ascent (drone) to the house on the Sure. Casting: team confirmed with staff releases; guests non-identifiable only; ambassador couple arranged by the hotel. Production: natural light, small crew, static frames and slow dollies for calm, handheld vertical for UGC; full rights all channels no time limit; delivery via Hautel Drive within 5 working days, 1 revision round.','drive/Cocoon Hotels/Hautel_Agency_Cocoon_UGC_EN.pdf'),
  (null,'e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009','brief','Opnameschema Cocoon Hotels: Elk zijn tempo (NL, Sep 2026)','Project: refresh van de visuele identiteit, brand film, UGC-content en fotopakket. Duur: 1 draaidag. Team: fotograaf, videograaf, dronepiloot. Doel: in een draaidag 6 deliverables (hero film, 4 UGC-capsules, fotopakket) met respect voor de operationele flow van het hotel; content voor OTA-profielen (Booking, Expedia), website, social media, Google Business Profile, brochures, persberichten en de contentdatabank. Rechten: volledige gebruiksrechten, alle kanalen, onbeperkt in tijd. Taal: UGC-capsules in het Frans gesproken met Engelse ondertitels; indien Frans niet mogelijk, Engels gesproken met Franse ondertitels. Schema: 08:00 opening b-roll ochtendlicht Sure en hotel, exterieurfoto''s; 08:30 trage wereld ouder koppel, ontbijtopstelling; 09:00 lezen en rust in lobby en terrassen; 09:30 UGC All about Cocoon met de representative; 10:00 transitie; 10:30 actief jong koppel fiets en tuin, parallel fotoblok kamers, cottages en villa na check-out om 11u; 12:30 UGC F&B gerecht; 13:45 UGC spa en wellness; 14:15 UGC cottages; 15:30 outdoor langs de Sure; 16:30 kruising lange tafel gouden uur; 17:30 finale drone avondbeeld. Fotopakket: 15-20 geretoucheerde kernbeelden plus reportagebeelden; alle verblijfstypes en kernruimtes; fotograaf werkt parallel met videograaf. Productieprincipes: discretie (gasten enkel niet-identificeerbaar tenzij toestemming), authenticiteit (echte gezichten van het huis), natuurlijk licht, een draaidag. Richtvragen per capsule: geen script, spontane antwoorden in eigen woorden.','drive/Cocoon Hotels/Opnameschema_Cocoon_Hotels_NL (1).pdf'),
  (null,'e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004','brief','Production briefing DoubleTree by Hilton Brussels City (30 Apr 2026, FR/EN)','Un hotel centenaire, une marque mondiale. Le Palace, Bruxelles, ouvert en 1910: 500 chambres a l''ouverture, seul hotel climatise de Belgique, 8 millions de briques, remparts medievaux decouverts en 1908, 70 000 bouteilles en cave; Grace Kelly, Bardot, le Prince Rainier de Monaco et le Roi Hussein de Jordanie y ont sejourne. L''extension en cours (grande salle de bal et espaces meetings) fera du DoubleTree Brussels City le deuxieme plus grand hotel de Belgique. Brand DNA DoubleTree by Hilton: marque upscale full-service dans plus de 60 pays; ''The Little Things Mean Everything''; culture C.A.R.E. (Create A Rewarding Experience); global standards, local soul; signatures: le cookie chaud a l''arrivee, Sweet Dreams sleep experience, restauration locale; palette signature navy, warm cookie, deep green, white, gold, charcoal; nouveau restaurant avec lustres et lumiere naturelle. La tension creative centrale: ce que l''hotel etait (un palais, royaute, legende) et ce qu''il devient (un hub corporate mondial, meetings et evenements internationaux). Approche: luxury at its core, corporate in purpose (la capsule meeting convainc un event planner en 30 secondes), cinematic in form (RED Komodo 6K, etalonnage cinema, chaque plan decide; pas une visite virtuelle, un film de marque). Tournage 3e-4e semaine de mai 2026, formats 16:9 et 9:16, livraison 7 jours. Outil de pre-visualisation: Weavy.ai. Client answers to the production questionnaire (22 May 2026): objective is to increase visibility and support the repositioning by visually communicating the transformation; audiences: event planners, corporate clients, international leisure travellers, sales missions; what stands out: the ecosystem of spaces under one roof (ballroom, Pagoda, breakout rooms, simultaneous events); feeling: human and personal, modern and international; selling points: natural light, high capacity, central location, technology and connectivity, unique F&B catering (the bowl concept as visual signature), sustainable initiatives; Art Deco influences, Swarovski-inspired elements in the ballroom, golden accents; staff open to non-speaking roles (front desk, chefs, bar, events and sales managers); constraints: availability and F&B limitations; all spaces camera-ready incl. lobby, restaurant, bar, ballroom, rooms, suites, wellness; must not feel too commercial or like previous hotel videos.','drive/DBT PROJECT/Briefing_Hautel_Doubletree2026-4.pdf; DoubleTree Brussels City Production Briefing (Responses)'),
  (null,'e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004','brief','Creative strategy: Le Palace, Where Time Waits (May 2026)','Deliverables: 1 presentation film 1''30 and 1 single capsule 30 s covering four locations (restaurant and bar, meeting rooms, guest rooms and suites, fitness and sauna). Production budget 2,000 EUR incl. VAT max, firm; shooting 1 day starting 1 PM with golden hour 3-5 PM; platforms website, YouTube, LinkedIn, corporate screens. Business objective: reposition Le Palace as a living heritage hotel, away from a commercial register into brand storytelling. Pursue: 100% cinematic, architecture as central character, real DoubleTree employees, sensory storytelling, perfect narrative loop. Avoid: commercial register, generic luxury cliches, performative acting, extras, explanatory voice-over. Synopsis: an architect under deadline pressure finds a 1910 photograph of Le Palace inscribed ''This place protects time''; his watch stops at 2:00 PM; at the hotel the Art Deco architecture, the staff and the period materials (brass, marble, velvet) give him what he needs before he asks; his project is complete; his watch restarts; final drone shot of the facade matching the 1910 photograph. Three acts (office 22 s, hotel 56 s, exit 12 s), 40-shot shotlist, sound design as second narrative voice with a hard cut to silence when the watch stops. Styling: architect 35-45 in 1910 vocabulary (jacquard waistcoat, morning coat, ivory cashmere scarf, black felt top hat); staff in period-inspired uniforms; palette deep black, ivory, flannel grey, bordeaux, aged gold, navy; no visible logos. References: Phantom Thread, In the Mood for Love, The Grand Budapest Hotel, La Grande Bellezza, Drive, Mr. Nobody; Chanel, Hermes, Cartier, Louis Vuitton films. Crew: director/art director included (agency), DP plus gimbal operator 400 EUR, stylist/props/production assistant 150 EUR, drone pilot 1 h 150 EUR, lead actor 250 EUR, light kit 200 EUR, costumes 200 EUR, props and catering, contingency 340 EUR. Pre-production checklist: location access, employee image consent, Brussels drone authorisation for the facade, casting, scout for the 1910 framing, weather plan B, fishing-line test for suspended papers, costume rental, staff briefing 30 min before.','drive/DBT PROJECT/Creative_Strategy_DoubleTree_LePalace_EN.pdf');
